title: APT Critical Updates
agents: linux
catalog: os/software
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the number of upgradable security packages on a Debian
 host. The data is collected by the agent plug-in {apt_updates}, which runs
 {apt list --upgradable} and counts packages whose name contains {-security}.

 Thresholds are configurable per host via the rule "APT critical updates".

item:
 None.

discovery:
 One service {APT Critical Updates} is created on every host that sends the
 {apt_updates} agent section.

